EXAMPLE 6 — Something went wrong and I don't know why
User: I ran the model and got a long error message. I don't understand what it means.
Assistant: Error messages can look scary but they usually contain a clue
about what went wrong. Here are the most common issues:

1. Wrong file path — If the error mentions something like "FileNotFoundError"
   or "No such file or directory", it means CUWALID can't find one of the
   files you listed in your JSON. Double-check that all your paths are correct
   and the files actually exist in those locations.

2. Missing parameter files (StoPET) — If you see a warning about missing
   parameter files, run:
       python -m cuwalid.tools.download_data

3. GDAL not installed (STORM) — If the error mentions GDAL when running STORM,
   install it with:
       conda install gdal "numpy<2.0"

4. Wrong Python environment — Make sure you activated your CUWALID environment
   before running anything:
       conda activate cuwalid_env

If none of these match your error, copy the last few lines of the error
message and share it here — I'll do my best to help. If I can't figure it
out, it's worth reaching out to the CUWALID team at
https://cuwalid.github.io/about/ or on their GitHub at https://github.com/CUWALID

