EXAMPLE 8 — Where can I learn DRYP step by step?
User: I want to learn how to use DRYP properly. Is there a tutorial I can follow?
Assistant: Yes! DRYP has a great set of hands-on training materials organised
into two modules — both are Jupyter Notebooks, which are interactive documents
where you read explanations, run code, and see results all in one place.

Module 1 — Understanding DRYP (great starting point):
  1. Introduction to the DRYP Python library:
     https://github.com/AndresQuichimbo/CUWALID-tutorials/blob/main/Training/DRYP/intro_modelling/01_DRYP_intro.ipynb
  2. Understanding the model grid environment:
     https://github.com/AndresQuichimbo/CUWALID-tutorials/blob/main/Training/DRYP/intro_modelling/02_DRYP_model_development.ipynb
  3. Exploring DRYP behaviour through synthetic experiments:
     https://github.com/AndresQuichimbo/CUWALID-tutorials/blob/main/Training/DRYP/intro_modelling/03_DRYP_test_models.ipynb

Module 2 — Building a real catchment model (once you're comfortable with the basics):
  1. Preparing input parameters and datasets (pre-processing):
     https://github.com/AndresQuichimbo/CUWALID-tutorials/blob/main/Training/DRYP/catchment/02_DRYP_pre_processing.ipynb
  2. Running a catchment-scale DRYP simulation:
     https://github.com/AndresQuichimbo/CUWALID-tutorials/blob/main/Training/DRYP/catchment/DRYP_model_running.ipynb
  3. Post-processing the model outputs:
     https://github.com/AndresQuichimbo/CUWALID-tutorials/blob/main/Training/DRYP/catchment/04_DRYP_post_processing.ipynb

I'd suggest starting with notebook 01 from Module 1 and working through them
in order. The overview page is also helpful:
https://cuwalid.github.io/tutorials/dryp-tutorial

