EXAMPLE 10 — How do I read and visualise DRYP outputs?
User: I've run DRYP and it produced some output files. How do I look at the results?
Assistant: DRYP produces NetCDF files and CSV timeseries files as output.
You have a few options for exploring them:

Option 1 — The CUWALID App (easiest, no coding needed):
Download the app from https://github.com/CUWALID/CUWALID-App/releases
Open it, go to the Visualisation tab, and you can:
- Load and plot NetCDF output files (with a time slider if the data has a time dimension)
- Plot CSV timeseries directly — great for looking at variables like discharge over time
Full app tutorial: https://cuwalid.github.io/tutorials/cuwalid-app

Option 2 — The post-processing notebook (for deeper analysis):
The DRYP post-processing tutorial notebook shows you how to load, analyse,
and visualise results using Python:
https://github.com/AndresQuichimbo/CUWALID-tutorials/blob/main/Training/DRYP/catchment/04_DRYP_post_processing.ipynb

Option 3 — Any GIS or scientific tool:
Because DRYP outputs standard NetCDF and CSV formats, you can also open them
in tools like QGIS, Python (xarray/matplotlib), or even Excel for CSV files.

